# Build CONTEXT for deploy/Dockerfile.runtime is the repo root, but only runtime/ is COPYd into
# the image. Exclude everything else + the heavy in-runtime SCRATCH so the context stays small and
# the daemon doesn't ship gigabytes it never uses. The lean runtime/compilers-dist/ (~640M, from
# scripts/stage-tools.sh) is NOT matched here and ships as the in-sandbox toolchain.

# --- repo dirs not needed by the runtime image ---
.git
.beads
desktop
web
**/node_modules
**/erl_crash.dump

# --- runtime/: rebuilt fresh in the image, so local copies are dead weight ---
runtime/_build
runtime/deps
runtime/.elixir_ls
runtime/tmp
runtime/wb
runtime/.publish_out
runtime/commands/*/target
runtime/kernel/target

# --- runtime-generated WASM scratch (content-addressed; the engine regenerates
# both on demand — same contract as build/cache). Was leaking ~766 MB into the
# CI/ghcr image (ci/Dockerfile.runtime) because the root .dockerignore — which
# governs the repo-root build context — never excluded them; only
# runtime/.dockerignore (the deploy-kit variant's context) did. Keep ONLY the
# named prebuilt externals (jq/grep) the engine does NOT synthesize. ---
runtime/build/cache
runtime/build/commands/*
!runtime/build/commands/jq.wasm
!runtime/build/commands/grep.wasm

# --- the ~6.6G provisioned compile-tool SCRATCH (rustc src, mrustc C++ build, wasi-sdk, .bak) ---
# Never run, only used to PRODUCE the wasm tools. The lean compilers-dist/ ships instead.
runtime/compilers

# cargo/rust build artifacts (wrong arch in-image; rebuilt) — esp. vendor/wasmex/native/*/target (~1.1G)
**/target

# stale prebuilt rustler NIF (host-arch .so) — force deps.compile to build the linux NIF + keep it
**/priv/native/*.so
